    Use Spring Security 5.7.12 for the LDAP bundle as well (#8219)
    
    All Spring Security bundles are 5.7.12, except spring-security-ldap,
    which was 5.8.6 since the upgrade to Spring Security 5. It only worked
    because the ServiceMix bundles import the Spring Security core packages
    without a version range, so nothing stops a 5.8 bundle from wiring to
    the 5.7 core.
    
    ServiceMix provides spring-security-ldap 5.7.12_4, the same rebuild as
    the other Spring Security bundles, and both 5.7.12 and 5.8.6 use the
    Spring LDAP 2.4.1 bundle we already ship. Use it, and replace the
    separate LDAP version properties and the hard-coded CAS bundle version
    with a single property for the ServiceMix Spring Security bundles.
    
    Upgrading everything to 5.8 instead would also have resolved the
    mismatch, but Karaf's spring-legacy feature repository ends with Spring
    Security 5.7.x. We would have to replace Karaf's spring-security feature
    with our own list of ServiceMix 5.8 bundles and their dependencies and
    maintain it ourselves, which is not worth it for a 5.x minor release.
    
    Tested LDAP against the public forumsys LDAP test server with identical
    results to 5.8.6: login through LDAP bind authentication, rejected
    logins for a wrong password and an unknown user, database login still
    working, and name, email and roles provided by the LDAP user directory.
    
    
